## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays, a common beginner challenge with practical reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- dp[i][t]: best sum using first i elements with exactly t subarrays
- end[i][t]: best subarray sum ending at i-1 for t subarrays
- Transitions combine extending a subarray or starting a new one
- Reconstruction via backtracking boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      end[i][t] = Math.max(end[i-1][t] + A[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], end[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n][k]};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for at-most-k subarrays?
- How would you retrieve the actual subarray boundaries efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests formulating a DP over partitions with a subarray-internal metric.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP
- Prefix sums
- Reconstruction pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP skeleton
function maxValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i]+A[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const cut = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) {
     for (let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++) {
        let maxVal = -Infinity; let bestP = -1; let curMax = -Infinity;
        for (let p=i-1; p>=t-1; p--) {
           curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[p]);
           const val = dp[p][t-1] + (pref[i]-pref[p]) - curMax;
           if (val>maxVal) { maxVal=val; bestP=p; }
        }
        dp[i][t] = maxVal; cut[i][t] = bestP;
     }
  }
  return {value: dp[n][k], cuts: cut};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What is the time complexity and how would you optimize to O(nk) with a deque?
- How would you reconstruct the exact subarray endpoints?

## Why This Is Asked
- Tests DP state design that tracks both position and budget (flips).
- Requires reconstruction to return exact indices, not just value.

## Key Concepts
- DP state with dual dimension (i, flips)
- Transition depends on current bit; reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesRun(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: k+1}, () => null));
  let bestLen = 0, bestEnd = 0, bestJ = 0;
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) {
    for (let j=0; j<=k; j++) {
      if (s[i] === '1') {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j] : null;
      } else if (j>0) {
        dp[i][j] = (i>0 ? dp[i-1][j-1] : 0) + 1;
        prev[i][j] = i>0 ? [i-1, j-1] : null;
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = 0; prev[i][j] = null;
      }
      if (dp[i][j] > bestLen) { bestLen = dp[i][j]; bestEnd = i; bestJ = j; }
    }
  }
  const start = bestEnd - bestLen + 2;
  return {bestLen, start, end: bestEnd+1, flips: bestJ};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reduce space to O(k)?
- How would you adapt if flips must happen in blocks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with a spacing constraint and path reconstruction, a common interview variation.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefix with constrained subsequences
- 2D state and reconstruction pointers
- Handling infeasible states and space-time trade-offs

## Code Example
